gametitle=Madden NFL 2004 (SLUS-20752) [14F8B841]
comment=P8 MOTION BLOCK -- drive the doubled defender back, weight+STR law. Over P1+P4.
// Design: docs/motion-block-cave.md. The agent REJECTED both proposed hooks on
// live evidence -- the defender's motion block holds stale float garbage for
// pair-family clips and writing it would fling him -- and relocated the
// applier's addition into the kind-8 helper servicer at 0x001F2164 (Site B,
// inside 0x001F20F8), which runs every attached frame. That makes 'drive only
// while the helper is touching' the law itself: TE alone gives R=0.825, D=0.
//
// Law: D = clamp(margin + R^2 - 1, 0, 3); slot 9 TE+RT vs DE R=1.8484, D=2.42,
// step 0.0378-0.0424 yd/frame. Gates: defender kind in {5,6}, defender
// dt_role==2, helper dt_role==1, sides differ, handle kind 1, and D<=0 writes
// nothing -- so band-0 pairs and every single block are byte-identical by
// construction, not by branch. Accumulates +0x190/+0x194 in place; +0x1A8
// (facing) untouched, so no warps and no spin.
//
// Cave #7 re-censused INDEPENDENTLY this pass: 0 data-word pointers, 0
// branches or jumps from outside, ELF byte-identical to slot 9's memory.
// Canary at 0x00514974 (ELF-zero, no patch line) increments per driven frame.
// Companion word admits clip 161 to the yes-set so the record outlives f64.

